Relevant columns and their potential usage  
------------------------------------------------
ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES  
• "from_address": identify the sender – used for outgoing statistics, fee payer, failure counts  
• "to_address": identify the receiver – used for incoming statistics, counterparties  
• "value": Wei transferred – used for ETH amount metrics (÷ 10¹⁸)  
• "trace_type": distinguishes normal calls, reward, create, suicide … – used for excluding/including rows (e.g. delegatecall) and for reward/contract‑create counts  
• "call_type": helps filter out delegatecall/callcode/staticcall when trace_type = 'call'  
• "status": success (1) / failure (0) – used for failure counts and for excluding failed transfers when computing balances  
• "error": non‑null means the sub‑trace failed, useful for diagnostics  
• "gas_used": gas actually spent – used for avg / std gas metrics  
• "gas": gas supplied – auxiliary for fee checks  
• "block_timestamp": activity dating & hour‑of‑day pattern (< 148 322 880 000 0000 for “before 2017‑01‑01”)  
• "block_number": optional alternative time filter  
• "reward_type": when trace_type = 'reward', flags block or uncle reward → reward_amount  
• "subtraces": sanity check when analysing call trees  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRANSACTIONS  
• "hash": join key to TRACES if fees are needed  
• "from_address": fee payer – subtract ( "gas_price" * "receipt_gas_used" ) from balance  
• "to_address": counterparty  
• "value": Wei; an alternative to TRACES for simple transfers  
• "gas_price", "receipt_gas_used": compute transaction fees in Wei  
• "receipt_status": success/failure gate  
• "block_timestamp": activity dating / hour‑of‑day  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TOKEN_TRANSFERS  
• "from_address": token sender – token_out_* metrics  
• "to_address": token receiver – token_in_* metrics  
• "token_address": ERC20 contract address – token type counters  
• "value": token amount / id (convert with SAFE_CAST when needed)  
• "block_timestamp": filter by date  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.CONTRACTS  
• "address": contract address (equals "to_address" in create traces)  
• "bytecode": take LENGTH(bytecode) to obtain "bytecode_size"  
• "block_timestamp": creation time filter (before 2017‑01‑01)  
• "is_erc20", "is_erc721": classify contracts (optional)  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.LOGS  
• "address": emitting contract – optional when cross‑checking token events  
• "topics", "data": decode events if deeper ERC20 analysis required  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.BLOCKS  
• "miner": block miner – cross‑check reward traces if needed  
• "timestamp": optional for reward dating  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000  -- all activity before 2017‑01‑01  
• "trace_type" = 'call' AND ("call_type" IS NULL OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall'))  
• "status" = 1  -- successful traces  
• "trace_type" = 'reward'  -- mining reward rows  
• "trace_type" = 'create'  -- contract creation rows  

Exploratory SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each)  
---------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: Sample of pre‑2017 successful call traces that transfer a non‑zero amount
SELECT 
    "block_timestamp",
    "from_address",
    "to_address",
    "value"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND ("call_type" IS NULL OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall'))
  AND "status" = 1
  AND "value" <> 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct addresses that received mining rewards before 2017
SELECT DISTINCT
    "to_address" AS "miner_address"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'reward'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Examples of contracts created before 2017 with their bytecode length
SELECT 
    "address",
    LENGTH("bytecode") AS "bytecode_size"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.CONTRACTS
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
ORDER BY "bytecode_size" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Failed outgoing traces (status = 0) before 2017
SELECT 
    "from_address",
    "to_address",
    "error",
    "value"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "status" = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Token transfers received by addresses before 2017
SELECT 
    "to_address",
    "token_address",
    "value",
    "block_timestamp"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TOKEN_TRANSFERS
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Count of unique token types each address sent before 2017 (top 20)
SELECT 
    "from_address",
    COUNT(DISTINCT "token_address") AS "sent_token_types"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TOKEN_TRANSFERS
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
GROUP BY "from_address"
ORDER BY "sent_token_types" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Average and standard deviation of gas_used for incoming call traces to each address (simple sample)
SELECT 
    "to_address",
    AVG("gas_used") AS "avg_gas_used",
    STDDEV("gas_used") AS "std_gas_used"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND ("call_type" IS NULL OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall'))
  AND "status" = 1
GROUP BY "to_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Daily activity count for a sample address (replace <ADDR> with real address)
SELECT 
    FLOOR("block_timestamp"/86400000000) AS "day_bucket",  -- rough day bucket (micro‑sec / 86 400 000 000)
    COUNT(*) AS "tx_count"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND ("from_address" = '<ADDR>' OR "to_address" = '<ADDR>')
GROUP BY "day_bucket"
ORDER BY "day_bucket"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Contract creation count per creator address before 2017
SELECT 
    "from_address" AS "creator",
    COUNT(*) AS "contract_create_count"
FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'create'
GROUP BY "from_address"
ORDER BY "contract_create_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Net ETH received (incoming minus outgoing) per address before 2017 using traces (ignoring fees for now)
SELECT 
    addr,
    (SUM(CASE WHEN dir = 'in'  THEN val ELSE 0 END) -
     SUM(CASE WHEN dir = 'out' THEN val ELSE 0 END)) / 1e18 AS "net_balance_eth"
FROM (
    SELECT "to_address"   AS addr, "value" AS val, 'in'  AS dir
    FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
    WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
      AND "trace_type" = 'call'
      AND ("call_type" IS NULL OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall'))
      AND "status" = 1
      AND "value" <> 0

    UNION ALL

    SELECT "from_address" AS addr, "value" AS val, 'out' AS dir
    FROM ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES
    WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
      AND "trace_type" = 'call'
      AND ("call_type" IS NULL OR "call_type" NOT IN ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall'))
      AND "status" = 1
      AND "value" <> 0
) t
GROUP BY addr
LIMIT 20;
```

