ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES  
• "from_address": identify the sender – used for outgoing statistics, fee payer, failure counts  
• "to_address": identify the receiver – used for incoming statistics, counterparties  
• "value": Wei transferred – used for ETH amount metrics (÷ 10¹⁸)  
• "trace_type": distinguishes normal calls, reward, create, suicide … – used for excluding/including rows (e.g. delegatecall) and for reward/contract‑create counts  
• "call_type": helps filter out delegatecall/callcode/staticcall when trace_type = 'call'  
• "status": success (1) / failure (0) – used for failure counts and for excluding failed transfers when computing balances  
• "error": non‑null means the sub‑trace failed, useful for diagnostics  
• "gas_used": gas actually spent – used for avg / std gas metrics  
• "gas": gas supplied – auxiliary for fee checks  
• "block_timestamp": activity dating & hour‑of‑day pattern (< 148 322 880 000 0000 for “before 2017‑01‑01”)  
